  "articleBody": "Getting your Aledo roof evaluated after rain damage can feel like a big deal, but a little preparation on your end can really help the process go smoothly. You want to make sure the roofing professionals can do their best work and give you the most accurate assessment. Being ready allows them to focus on the technical details and get you answers faster, helping you protect your home from further damage.\n\n**What to Prepare Before You Start**\n\n- [ ] **Clear Access to Your Attic** — why this matters: If your roof is leaking, water often shows up in the attic first. Clearing a path and making sure the attic access is easily reachable helps the evaluator check for signs of moisture, mold, and structural damage in concealed spaces. This is key for tracing the leak's path.\n- [ ] **Gather Any Previous Roof Records** — why this matters: Having documents like your last roof inspection report, installation dates, or repair history can give the evaluator valuable context about your roof's age and past issues, helping them distinguish new storm damage from older deterioration.\n- [ ] **Note Down All Visible Damage** — why this matters: Make a list of everything you've noticed – drips, stains on ceilings, loose shingles you can see from the ground. This helps direct the evaluator's attention to areas of concern and ensures nothing is overlooked, especially if the leak is intermittent.\n- [ ] **Take Dated Photographs of Interior Leaks** — why this matters: Photos of interior water stains or active leaks, especially with a date stamp, provide concrete evidence of the damage. This can be particularly useful if the leak isn't active during the evaluation or for insurance purposes.\n- [ ] **Ensure Clear Exterior Perimeter** — why this matters: Make sure there's clear space around your house, free of obstacles like trash cans, garden tools, or parked cars. This allows the roofing team to safely set up ladders and move around the perimeter for a full exterior inspection without obstruction.\n\n**How to use this checklist**\nGo through these items before your scheduled evaluation. It's about empowering the professionals to do their best work and ensuring you get the most comprehensive assessment possible for your Aledo home. Discounted Roofing Co. aims to make the process as straightforward as possible for you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}